From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 05:42:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 22/34] coherent: per-range marks, host reads and writes,
 untracked and cross-device readers, signals

- Pages::track holds [start, start + len) as a range of its own (QEMU's census now does too, audit
  B1); the lanes' Fake models ranges, and a touch past the rows leaves the surface trapping.
- shadow_coherent::host_reads / host_writes: a host reader outside any command buffer (Reims'
  video, scaler, JPEG) syncs first; a host writer opens the surface as a CPU write (audit P1).
- met_by sees untracked uses (Summary::lazy_uses, audit P2) and a reader on another device by the
  host bytes its buffers lie over.
- A shared event's signal copies back what the command buffer's encoders left ahead first: a CPU
  waiter reads the pages before the completion arms them.
- A surface whose texture went retires (syncs, untracks) when a new texture over its pages comes,
  so the new one traps instead of copying back per encoder for good.
- flush: a copy back that finds nothing left after before_flush unmarks the copy in flight.
- CoherentFallbackCounts in WorkCounts::coherent: every silent fallback and host access, counted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
